          tags$b("AUC basis"), " control at the top of this tab (stated exactly in the blue note above). The Metrics tab also reports AUC (pre-baseline, dil-scaled). Values are integrated signal area in the declared wavelength window and processing basis; they do not identify or quantify a pigment without an applicable calibration or absorption coefficient and matched path length, matrix, blank, instrument response, and linear Beer–Lambert-compatible conditions. Normalized AUC describes relative shape/distribution on the normalized basis. Several default windows overlap (e.g. Soret and ",
